561677610,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjU0NDg2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3497#issuecomment-506544867"},"message":"So, based on that backtrace, the S3 special remote gets all the way to the end of `_publish_dataset()`:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/2cf1942819f9433ded6d28bfebcaee7296af78a8/datalad/distribution/publish.py#L452-L454\n\nI would have expected it to be caught about 50 lines back in that same function by this guard:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/2cf1942819f9433ded6d28bfebcaee7296af78a8/datalad/distribution/publish.py#L394-L400\n\nSo `repo.is_special_annex_remote()` must be returning false.\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/2cf1942819f9433ded6d28bfebcaee7296af78a8/datalad/support/annexrepo.py#L710-L723\n\nThat relies on `\u003cremote\u003e.annex-externaltype` or `\u003cremote\u003e.annex-webdav` being present, which I guess isn't sufficient to detect special remotes (assuming your S3 remote is set up correctly).  What do the config values look like for your special remote?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1561727883,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjczMDQ3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3497#issuecomment-506730472"},"message":"@kyleam:\n\n\u003e That relies on `\u003cremote\u003e.annex-externaltype` or `\u003cremote\u003e.annex-webdav` being present\n\nPoking around the git-annex source tree, it seems that (unsurprisingly) `externaltype` doesn't apply to internal git-annex special remotes.  I don't think there is a common feature of special remote config sections aside from that they do not have a URL.  So I think is_special_annex_remote() should either rely on that or use get_special_remotes(), as suggested at https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/1644#discussion_r130156986","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"f7ee2a4a03084a58d1d6d029a36a183aa3510117"},"timestamp":1561729381,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjczODc3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3497#issuecomment-506738775"},"message":"Thanks for all the help in this @kyleam. I'm still working through your comments. For now regarding the possibility of config being wrong here is the contents of .git/config (on a rerun of the above example):\n```\n[core]\n\trepositoryformatversion = 0\n\tfilemode = true\n\tbare = false\n\tlogallrefupdates = true\n\tignorecase = true\n\tprecomposeunicode = true\n[annex]\n\tuuid = c87831be-0331-40ca-8408-9d40e5d66680\n\tversion = 5\n\tbackends = MD5E\n[remote \"s3test2\"]\n\tannex-s3 = true\n\tannex-uuid = 815e1611-648c-4350-989c-be23438275fd\n\tannex-ignore = false\n[remote \"github\"]\n\tannex-ignore = true\n\turl = git@github.com:leej3/test_s3test2.git\n\tfetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/github/*\n\tdatalad-publish-depends = s3test2\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1561731083,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjc0ODQ1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3497#issuecomment-506748451"},"message":"\u003e here is the contents of .git/config\n\nThanks.   Indeed that is missing the keys is_special_annex_remote() currently looks for.  \n\nBased on your version info, I think you're installing from pypi, but if you also have datalad cloned locally, I'd be interested to know if the below patch works for you.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/datalad/support/annexrepo.py b/datalad/support/annexrepo.py\nindex 848de34e2..c853ed744 100644\n--- a/datalad/support/annexrepo.py\n+++ b/datalad/support/annexrepo.py\n@@ -950,10 +950,7 @@ def is_special_annex_remote(self, remote, check_if_known=True):\n             if remote not in self.get_remotes():\n                 raise RemoteNotAvailableError(remote)\n         sec = 'remote.{}'.format(remote)\n-        for opt in ('annex-externaltype', 'annex-webdav'):\n-            if self.config.has_option(sec, opt):\n-                return True\n-        return False\n+        return not self.config.has_option(sec, 'url')\n \n     @borrowkwargs(GitRepo)\n     def get_remotes(self,\n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1561996130,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI0NTE2ODEzMzc="},"added":["windows"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1561996153,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI0NTE2ODI0NDg="},"added":["fails-on-appveyor"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562603372,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwOTI5NzMzMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3500#issuecomment-509297331"},"message":"I suspect this is all due to the `find --json` [issue] in annex.  AppVeyor is [now running][ag] with a git-annex that includes the upstream fix, so we should find out on the next AppVeyor run for master.\n\n[issue]: http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/Regression_in___96__find_--json__96___output/\n[ag]: https://ci.appveyor.com/project/mih/datalad/builds/25824403/job/y2k9g724mwqar0dc#L544","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562603384,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MjQ2Njc0OTAxNA=="},"added":[],"removed":["windows"]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562603384,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI0NjY3NDkwMTY="},"added":["external-tools"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562605017,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwOTMwNjk2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3500#issuecomment-509306960"},"message":"\u003e so we should find out on the next AppVeyor run for master.\n\